<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicocreon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 311 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicocreon was the last king of Salamis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, ruling from about 332 BCE. He supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-i-soter">Ptolemy I</a> in the wars of the Successors, and Ptolemy made him general of Cyprus in 312 BCE. After his death around 311 BCE, Salamis came under direct Ptolemaic rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicocreon.jpg" alt="Nicocreon" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:LouisAragon (uploader) · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Nikokreon_of_Cyprus_following_Persian_standard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
